From 4527361cdb2c9214b61d1baa0a751096559ada6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 10:50:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09687/11362] [outer-loop] Reaper fix round 2: six sweeps
 covered, per-pid multi-GPU gate, prev-log evidence (REQ-INFRA-079)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adversarial review of the first round found the fix's own enumeration
pattern-narrower-than-concept. Landed, each proven by deletion (7 mutations
RED, restores byte-identical):

- scripts/gpu_monitor.py: server exemption in detect_zombies. This sweep runs
  LIVE (dry_run=False) in every conductor task pre-check with a cumulative
  cpu/wall < 1% proxy that matches a mostly-idle server by construction — an
  uneliminated co-candidate for the supab5 kills, recorded as such in
  known-issues (the "elimination of every other candidate" claim is corrected
  there, append-only).
- gemma_isolation step-3 residual sweep + vram_loop_eviction retry loop:
  server skip, so the primary pass's exemption is not defeated lines below it.
- experiment_template: BOTH paths now decide per PID with MAX utilization
  across the pid's own GPUs (a process busy on one GPU is not killable via
  its idle-GPU line); pynvml path restructured two-pass and now actually
  under test via a faked pynvml module (review proved the prior exemption
  there decorative — every earlier test forced pynvml absent).
- markers: + "vllm serve" CLI form everywhere.
- arc_executable_world_model: death-signature hint also reads the PREVIOUS
  server log (after kill+relaunch the evidence lives in the old log); wording
  softened to "termination signal" — llama-server prints the same lines for a
  self-sent SIGTERM; bounded tail read via seek.
- spec REQ-INFRA-079: statement now lists all six sweeps and binds new sweeps
  to join the list or carry a written exemption reason.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
